Hello,

I am using an ASUS WL-500gPv1 router (Broadcom 4704 + Broadcom 4318)
running Openwrt (2.6 + b43).
After upgrading to 2.6.27 and compat-wireless-2008-10 ssh (and samba)
sessions through wireless to the router hang after a short while
(seconds to minutes). The problem is the same since (2.6.27.7 +
compat-wireless-2008-11-22 + hostapd 0.6.5).
Interestingly, if I connect to a computer plugged into the router
first (through the WLAN of the router) and then ssh to the router from
that computer then the problem does not occur.

Looking at the packets captured by Wireshark (attached), something
seems to be wrong with lost packets / packet retransmissions (packet
loss is about 1-3%)

Please tell me howto resolve this problem, or what I could do to help
resolving it (I am not a programmer).

